The two-point neighbourhood system has the two-element set as its tokens, the singleton of zero and the full two-point set as its only neighbourhoods, and the full set as its master. Zero belongs to the master, and the master is the second neighbourhood. The intersection of two neighbourhoods is the singleton whenever either factor is the singleton, using the inclusion of the singleton in the full set, and is the full set when both factors are the full set. The singleton is contained in the full set, and the full set is contained in itself.
